# Phase 8: exclusions for the inference-service Docker build context.
# Rationale is documented per-section — this is not a blind "exclude
# everything" copy-paste.

# --- Raw dataset: large (~1.3GB), not needed for inference. The
# pretrained model bundle (data/interim/phase6_model_bundle.pkl, NOT
# excluded below) already encodes everything training needed from it.
# Excluding this also keeps the Dockerfile from ever being tempted to
# "just retrain" using data baked into the image.
data/raw/
data/processed/

# --- Prior-phase JSON metrics/metadata (small individually, but numerous
# and irrelevant to serving predictions). Does NOT match the .pkl model
# bundle, which is copied explicitly by the Dockerfile.
data/interim/*.json

# --- Generated figures from earlier phases' reports — large PNGs with no
# runtime purpose.
reports/figures/
reports/*.csv

# --- Exploration notebooks — not runtime code.
notebooks/

# --- Tests — not needed to SERVE the API; the Dockerfile does not copy
# this directory, and this entry is a defensive backstop in case that
# changes later.
tests/

# --- Python / tooling artifacts
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- Local environments / VCS / editor
.git/
.gitignore
.venv/
venv/
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- Local secrets/config — never bake real environment values into the
# image; .env.example is the documented template, not a real .env file.
.env
!.env.example

# --- Misc local artifacts that may exist in a dev sandbox but should
# never end up in a built image.
swapfile
*.log
